# JustDubit Interface & Model Acquisition

This plan outlines the creation of a premium web interface for the video dubbing pipeline and the process for downloading the necessary multi-gigabyte model weights.

## User Review Required

## Prerequisites

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Local FFmpeg Required**: This project relies on `ffmpeg` for audio extraction and video encoding. You must have `ffmpeg` installed and available in your system's PATH. This is essential for the 100% offline processing to work.
>
> **100% Offline Processing**: Once the models and FFmpeg are ready, all processing occurs entirely on your local GPU. No data leaves your machine.
>
> **Local Translation**: JustDubit uses the local Gemma model to encode prompts. To translate from non-English to English, the interface will provide options to generate the appropriate prompt.
>
> **Language Detection**: JustDubit is an audio-visual generation model. It doesn't "autodetect" the source language for translation automatically; instead, it generates the target language based on the prompt provided. I will implement a local Whisper-based detection or a simple language selector to assist with this.

> [!WARNING]
> **Lite Footprint Refinement**: To address your space concerns, I have switched to a **"Lite" configuration**:
> 1. **Removed Stage 2 Upsampling**: This skips the High-Res refinement (~6GB saving).
> 2. **Smaller Text Encoder**: Switched from Gemma 12B (~23GB) to **Gemma 4B (~8GB)**.
> 3. **Estimated Total**: ~25GB total footprint (instead of 60GB+).
> 4. **Local Cleanup**: All weights will be stored in `c:\just-dub-it\weights`. Deleting this folder removes the project entirely.
>
> **LM-Studio Integration**: I will attempt to source the Gemma model from your local `LM-Studio\LLM cache` first if compatible formats are found.

## Proposed Changes

### Web Interface (FastAPI + React)
- **Backend (Python)**:
  - Create a FastAPI server (`server.py`) to handle file uploads and trigger the inference pipeline.
  - Implement local Whisper integration for optional automated transcript generation from source video.
  - Implement a websocket or polling mechanism to provide real-time status updates from the pipeline.
### [Backend] (server.py)
- [NEW] Global `job_queue` and management logic to handle sequential processing.
- [NEW] `kill_job` endpoint to signal cancellation to the active runner.
- Implementation of `threading.Event`-based cancellation tokens for the diffusion pipeline.
- Pass the `device` parameter to the underlying pipeline.

